^SAMPLE = GSM8603678
!Sample_title = SBC5_WT
!Sample_geo_accession = GSM8603678
!Sample_status = Public on Oct 21 2025
!Sample_submission_date = Oct 30 2024
!Sample_last_update_date = Oct 21 2025
!Sample_type = SRA
!Sample_channel_count = 1
!Sample_source_name_ch1 = SBC5
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell line: SBC5
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = cell type: Small cell lung cancer
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = genotype: WT
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = treatment: CTRL
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = shHDAC3 cells were generated using lentiviral transduction and three independent shRNA constructs agains HDAC3. RGFP966 treatment was used by dissolving RGFP966 in DMSO and diluting in a vehihcle of 40% (v/v) polyethylene glycol 300 (TCI Chemicals # H0543), 5% (v/v) TWEEN 80 (Sigma-Aldrich # P1754), and 45% (v/v) saline (Baxter # JF7123) to a final DMSO concentration of 10% (v/v).
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = SBC5 cells were cultured in Roswell Park Memorial Institute (RPMI) 1640 1X, (Wisent Bioproducts, catalog # 350-000-CL) and 10% FBS.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = genomic DNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = For each submitted sample, 60 000 viable cells were pelleted at 500 x g for 5 minutes at 4oC, resuspended in 50 µL of fully supplemented ATAC-seq resuspension buffer (RSB) containing 0.1% NP-40, 0.1% Tween-20, and 0.01% digitonin, and incubated on ice for 3 minutes. Following lysis, 1 mL of ATAC-seq RSB containing 0.1% Tween-20 (without NP-40 or digitonin) was added and the tubes were inverted to mix. Nuclei were then centrifuged at 500 x g for 10 minutes at 4oC, followed by careful aspiration of all supernatant and resuspension of pellet with 50 µL of transposition master mix (25 µL 2x TD buffer, 2.5 µL transposase, 16.5 µL PBS, 0.5 µL 1% digitonin, 0.5 µL 10% Tween-20, and 5 µL water).
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Transposition reactions were incubated at 37oC for 30 minutes in a thermomixer with shaking at 1000 rpm. Reactions were cleaned up with MinElute columns (Qiagen, catalog # 28204), followed by library amplification, where the appropriate number of PCR cycles was determined by qPCR. PCR product purification and size selection were achieved using AMPure XP Beads (Beckman Coulter, catalog # A63882).
!Sample_data_processing = Reads were aligned to human genome hg38 using Bowtie2 (v. 2.4.5) and filtered to remove multimapping reads using Sambamba (v. 0.7.0).
!Sample_data_processing = Samtools (v. 1.14) was used to shift the read start sites (forward reads +4 bases, reverse reads -5 bases) to adjust for overhangs generated by the Tn5 transposon
!Sample_data_processing = Duplicate reads were flagged and removed using Picard MarkDuplicates (v. 2.10.9).
!Sample_data_processing = Peaks were called using MACS2 (v. 2.2.7.1) using a q-value cutoff of 0.01.
!Sample_data_processing = Bigwig files were generated using deeptools bamCoverage (v. 3.5.1) normalizing to reads per kilobase per million (RPKM) and a bin size of 10 bases.
!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: hg38
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: MACS2 narrowPeak files
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: RPKM-normalized bigwig files for each sample and mean coverage for each condition.
!Sample_platform_id = GPL24676
!Sample_contact_name = Benjamin,H,Lok
!Sample_contact_institute = Princess Margaret Cancer Centre
!Sample_contact_address = 101 College Street, PMCRT, 13-307
!Sample_contact_city = Toronto
!Sample_contact_state = ON
!Sample_contact_zip/postal_code = M5G1L7
!Sample_contact_country = Canada
!Sample_instrument_model = Illumina NovaSeq 6000
!Sample_library_selection = other
!Sample_library_source = genomic
!Sample_library_strategy = ATAC-seq
!Sample_relation = BioSample: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/biosample/SAMN44510297
!Sample_relation = SRA: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sra?term=SRX26551698
!Sample_supplementary_file_1 = ftp://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo/samples/GSM8603nnn/GSM8603678/suppl/GSM8603678_001WT.bw
